Create agnt-gg platform API tool files for the consolidated package at `/Users/ajaxdavis/repos/tpmjs/tpmjs/packages/tools/official/agnt/src/`.

These tools wrap the agnt-gg platform REST API. The base URL comes from `AGNT_API_URL` env var, and auth from `AGNT_API_KEY` env var.

Use the same AI SDK v6 pattern as the existing tools in the same directory. Here's the pattern:

```typescript
import { jsonSchema, tool } from 'ai';

export const myTool = tool({
  description: 'Description',
  inputSchema: jsonSchema<InputType>({
    type: 'object',
    properties: { ... },
    required: [...],
    additionalProperties: false,
  }),
  execute: async (input): Promise<OutputType> => { ... },
});
```

Create these files:

### 1. `src/platform.ts` - Core platform tools

Shared helpers at top:
```typescript
function getConfig() {
  const apiUrl = process.env.AGNT_API_URL;
  if (!apiUrl) throw new Error('AGNT_API_URL env var is required');
  const apiKey = process.env.AGNT_API_KEY;
  if (!apiKey) throw new Error('AGNT_API_KEY env var is required');
  return { apiUrl: apiUrl.replace(/\/$/, ''), apiKey };
}

async function agntRequest<T>(method: string, path: string, body?: unknown): Promise<T> {
  const { apiUrl, apiKey } = getConfig();
  const response = await fetch(`${apiUrl}${path}`, {
    method,
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      'Authorization': `Bearer ${apiKey}`,
    },
    ...(body ? { body: JSON.stringify(body) } : {}),
  });
  if (!response.ok) {
    const text = await response.text().catch(() => '');
    throw new Error(`Agnt API error (${response.status}): ${text || response.statusText}`);
  }
  return response.json() as Promise<T>;
}
```

Tools to create (all exported as named exports):

**Agents:**
- `listAgents` - GET /api/agents/ - returns list of agents
- `getAgent` - GET /api/agents/:id - returns agent details, input: { agentId: string }
- `createAgent` - POST /api/agents/save - input: { name: string, description?: string, model?: string, provider?: string, systemPrompt?: string, tools?: string } (tools is JSON string of tool array)
- `updateAgent` - PUT /api/agents/:id - input: { agentId: string, name?: string, description?: string, model?: string, provider?: string, systemPrompt?: string, tools?: string }
- `deleteAgent` - DELETE /api/agents/:id - input: { agentId: string }
- `chatWithAgent` - POST /api/agents/:id/chat - input: { agentId: string, message: string, conversationId?: string }

**Workflows:**
- `listWorkflows` - GET /api/workflows/ - returns list of workflows
- `getWorkflow` - GET /api/workflows/:id - input: { workflowId: string }
- `createWorkflow` - POST /api/workflows/save - input: { name: string, description?: string, nodes?: string, edges?: string } (nodes/edges are JSON strings)
- `deleteWorkflow` - DELETE /api/workflows/:id - input: { workflowId: string }
- `startWorkflow` - POST /api/workflows/:id/start - input: { workflowId: string, inputData?: string } (inputData is JSON string)
- `stopWorkflow` - POST /api/workflows/:id/stop - input: { workflowId: string }
- `getWorkflowStatus` - GET /api/workflows/:id/status - input: { workflowId: string }

**Generate:**
- `generateWorkflow` - POST /api/streams/generate-workflow - input: { description: string, provider?: string, model?: string }
- `generateAgent` - POST /api/streams/generate-agent - input: { description: string, provider?: string, model?: string }

**Goals:**
- `listGoals` - GET /api/goals/ - returns list of goals
- `createGoal` - POST /api/goals/create - input: { name: string, description: string, agentId?: string, steps?: string } (steps is JSON string)
- `executeGoal` - POST /api/goals/:id/execute - input: { goalId: string }
- `getGoalStatus` - GET /api/goals/:id/status - input: { goalId: string }
- `deleteGoal` - DELETE /api/goals/:id - input: { goalId: string }

**Orchestrator:**
- `orchestratorChat` - POST /api/orchestrator/chat - input: { message: string, context?: string } (context is JSON string)

**Executions:**
- `listExecutions` - GET /api/executions/ - returns execution list
- `getExecution` - GET /api/executions/:id - input: { executionId: string }

**Custom Tools:**
- `listCustomTools` - GET /api/custom-tools/ - returns custom tool list
- `createCustomTool` - POST /api/custom-tools/save - input: { name: string, description: string, schema?: string, code?: string } (schema/code are JSON strings)
- `deleteCustomTool` - DELETE /api/custom-tools/:id - input: { toolId: string }

Every tool must have:
- Exported interface for input and result types (use generic result types like `AgntAgent`, `AgntWorkflow`, etc.)
- `additionalProperties: false` on the jsonSchema
- `description` on every property
- try-catch in execute
- Named export

At the end, export a default object containing all tools:
```typescript
export default { listAgents, getAgent, createAgent, ... };
```

Make sure to define reasonable interfaces for the return types (AgntAgent, AgntWorkflow, AgntGoal, AgntExecution, etc.) - they don't need to be exact, just reasonable representations. Export all interfaces.

